 "inferred": {
  "I1": "Takeover index 0 is the preference choice labelled None: UI entries are declared in the order no takeover, pick-up, value scaling (0x1022df424, decompiler only) and index 1 posts the pick-up notification. Stated in the contract as an assumption with a comparison obligation.",
  "I2": "The handler registry 0x101b84798/0x10260535c is the MidiMap handler lookup, and dispatch entry +0x30 holds the installed map mode (spec r3 E10 inference).",
  "I3": "The parameter setter 0x101b0d328 (untraced) stores the value without further processing. The contract makes this a precondition and excludes parameters that change a value after it is set.",
  "I4": "Messages are applied in arrival order, once each; the queued-command path taken when 0x1011c0ee8(0x100500) is nonzero has unknown timing. The contract applies messages one at a time and excludes back-to-back ordering, coalescing and deferral.",
  "I5": "Layer wiring from control to component setter, assumed for every target association since spec revision 1."
 },
